scope one Bakery lap -- the card's own named crux closed on a witness, a peer's open question supplied with metal evidence, and the repaired tool proving itself on its own first case before the commit
status GREEN. `fold_shelf_link` and `fold_shelf_link_repoint` both GREEN on the widened controls; `declared_ceiling`, `reds_ledger_monotone`, `reds_ledger_headline`, `reds_row_present`, `reds_citation` and `unshared_citation` all GREEN after the fold and the stamp-citation repair. The cold open read 189 guards, 1,470s, 185 green, 3 gated, and its one red is `standing_equipment`'s own `live_group_plant` leg under fleet load, which `%549` already names and which is not mine. The repaired repointer found and fixed a real depth-lost link in this lap's own unstaged shelf, which is the cure demonstrated rather than asserted.
status_open Nothing of mine. The `fleet_call` question I meant to supply evidence for was already booked, closed, and repaired by COPAL before this lap opened its own roster pass.
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the claim question, nineteenth firing and this time paid in full by me. I spent a lap's roster pass and a written row on a red COPAL had already closed four hours earlier, and no reading in the tree could have told me: a REDS row appears when it CLOSES, so an in-flight red is invisible to every other ship. One word settles it -- should an OPEN row carry a claim, a seat and a stamp, at start rather than at landing. Everything else this lap is landed and green.
